{"id": "EUVD-2026-102942", "enisaUuid": "a4c520fc-624e-3e30-8f80-16cc587b4652", "description": "MariaDB server is a community developed fork of MySQL server. From 10.6.1 until 10.6.28, 10.11.19, 11.4.13, 11.8.9, 12.3.3, and 13.0.2, ST_Area reads beyond the allocated buffer when processing invalid WKB for a MultiPolygon because the multi-polygon parser advances past a nested geometry header without first verifying enough input remains. A low-privileged remote attacker can supply malformed spatial data to disclose memory useful for bypassing ASLR as part of a multi-vulnerability chain. This issue is fixed in versions 10.6.28, 10.11.19, 11.4.13, 11.8.9, 12.3.3, and 13.0.2.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T16:30:30", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T12:39:16", "baseScore": 4.3, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N", "references": ["https://github.com/MariaDB/server/security/advisories/GHSA-p7v9-24h4-mch8", "https://github.com/MariaDB/server/commit/2bf355e361db85153fdfba7b8a0f0d114d6a26ce", "https://github.com/MariaDB/server/releases/tag/mariadb-10.11.19", "https://github.com/MariaDB/server/releases/tag/mariadb-10.6.28", "https://github.com/MariaDB/server/releases/tag/mariadb-11.4.13", "https://github.com/MariaDB/server/releases/tag/mariadb-11.8.9", "https://github.com/MariaDB/server/releases/tag/mariadb-12.3.3", "https://github.com/MariaDB/server/releases/tag/mariadb-13.0.2", "https://jira.mariadb.org/browse/MDEV-40328"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-85745"], "assigner": "GitHub_M", "epss": 0.34, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "34c325cb-b8e5-3d45-a5db-90b1a8c06824", "product": {"name": "Server", "vendor": {"name": "Devolutions"}}, "product_version": "10.11.1, < 10.11.19"}, {"id": "44025824-9156-338f-bdf7-f420a5611222", "product": {"name": "Server", "vendor": {"name": "Devolutions"}}, "product_version": "11.4.1, < 11.4.13"}, {"id": "4716d7f0-d9f4-3ab0-bc68-bee41fae392a", "product": {"name": "Server", "vendor": {"name": "Devolutions"}}, 